.nh
.TH "GMB" "1" "Sep 2026" "GlassMarble 1.2.0" "GlassMarble Manual"

.SH NAME
gmb-docserve - Run the doc engine as a daemon, updating docs on every file change


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgmb docserve [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Loads the documentation engine once and watches the repository for
file-system changes (fsnotify). Changes are coalesced through a debounce
window and each batch triggers one doc-engine update run.

.PP
Failures inside a batch update are logged as warnings and never abort the
daemon: the next batch retries on fresh state.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--debounce-ms\fP=2000
	Debounce window in milliseconds for coalescing file events

.PP
\fB--dir\fP="."
	Target repository directory

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for docserve

.PP
\fB--no-llm\fP[=false]
	Use deterministic renderer only (offline mode); skips the LLM readiness gate

.PP
\fB--workers\fP=2
	Number of batch-consumer workers (onChange never runs concurrently)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	Color output mode: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	Config file path (default is $HOME/.glassmarble.yaml)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging

.PP
\fB--max-json-mb\fP=0
	Refuse to load or commit an AKG state file (akg.json) larger than this many MiB (0 = unlimited)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-error output

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Verbose output logging


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Serve docs for the current repository
  gmb docserve

  # Watch a specific directory with a shorter debounce window
  gmb docserve --dir ./backend --debounce-ms 500 --workers 4
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgmb(1)\fP


